# .graphifyignore — what stays out of the knowledge graph.
#
# Syntax is gitignore's, in full:
#   #  comment          blank lines ignored
#   /  trailing         directory only  (models/)
#   /  leading/embedded anchors to this file's directory  (/models, src/*.log)
#   *  matches within one path segment, never across /
#   ** crosses path segments  (models/**/*.mp3)
#   !  re-includes a previously excluded path; last match wins
#
# graphify merges this with .gitignore — .gitignore is read first, this file
# last, so a rule here overrides one there. Two limits worth knowing:
#   * a `!` here cannot rescue a file whose parent directory is excluded
#     (list the file's own path instead of negating inside a dropped dir);
#   * .graphifyinclude is no longer supported — `!` below is the only way back.
#
# The lists are deliberately self-contained rather than leaning on .gitignore,
# so editing .gitignore never silently changes what the graph covers.

# ==================== Program models and media assets ====================
# Runtime DATA the app loads, not logic it runs: map definitions, colour-coded
# zone maps, print templates, the trained tap-classifier weights, and the
# narration audio. This is 84 of the repo's 119 files (57 mp3, 14 png, 3 jpg,
# the model JSONs) and yields no code structure — the model JSONs already
# extracted to zero nodes. Dropping them keeps the graph about the code.
models/
MP3/

# Collected tap samples used to retrain the classifier (dataset, not code)
data/

# README illustrations of the pointing gesture
img/

# To pull one map definition back in for its zone -> audio mapping, name the
# file itself — a `!` inside the excluded models/ directory would not apply:
# !models/UkraineMap/UkraineMap.json

